.TH PTY_WAIT_REGION 3 2026-10-03 "libptytest 0.1" "libptytest Manual"
.SH NAME
pty_wait_region, pty_wait_region_style \- wait for an exact picture of a
region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <ptytest.h>
.PP
.BI "int pty_wait_region(PtySession *" s ", const PtyRegion *" reg ,
.BI "                    const char *const " expected "[], int " timeout_ms ,
.BI "                    char *" report ", size_t " report_size );
.BI "int pty_wait_region_style(PtySession *" s ", const PtyRegion *" reg ,
.BI "                          const char *const " expected "[],"
.BI "                          const PtyStyleKey " legend "[], int " timeout_ms ,
.BI "                          char *" report ", size_t " report_size );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pty_wait_region ()
reads the program's output until the region
.I reg
(NULL: the whole screen) equals
.I expected
exactly, as
.BR pty_region_compare (3)
defines it, or until
.I timeout_ms
milliseconds have passed or the child has closed the PTY.
Then it compares once more, writing the report into
.IR report .
.PP
It is the wait to use when
.BR pty_wait_for (3)
would return too early: a view drawn in several writes satisfies a wait
for one of its words before it is complete, and a view that replaces
another with the same words in it satisfies it before it is drawn at all.
An exact picture is satisfied by nothing else.
And when it is not satisfied, the report says how the screen differs at
the deadline \(em which is the reason the wait failed, where a timed-out
.BR pty_wait_for (3)
can only say that the text did not come.
.PP
.BR pty_wait_region_style ()
does the same for a style map, as
.BR pty_region_compare_style (3)
defines it.
.PP
An expectation that cannot match at all (a region outside the screen, a
row wider than the region, a key missing from the legend) returns at
once instead of waiting out the timeout.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 if the region matched in time.
Otherwise the result of the final comparison: the number of differing
rows, or \-1 for an invalid region or expectation (also for a NULL
.I legend
in
.BR pty_wait_region_style ()).
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
pty_send_key(s, PTY_KEY_ENTER);

PtyRegion dialog = PTY_REGION(8, 20, 5, 40);
dialog.label = "confirm dialog";
const char *const expected[] = {
    "┌ Delete 3 messages? ──────────────────┐",
    "│                                      │",
    "│        [ Yes ]        [ No ]         │",
    "│                                      │",
    "└──────────────────────────────────────┘",
    NULL
};
ASSERT_WAIT_REGION(s, dialog, expected, 3000);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pty_region_compare (3),
.BR pty_wait_for (3),
.BR pty_assert (3)
